# The vendored mirror is identified by hash, so it must survive a checkout
# byte-for-byte. `scripts/vendor_openhack.py` records a sha256 of each file's
# bytes and `tests/test_vendor.py` re-reads those bytes, so any end-of-line
# translation between the two makes every hash wrong at once.
#
# Git's default is to translate, and `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows
# default — rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. The result is not a stray test
# failure: on the platform this is developed on, a *fresh clone* ships a
# manifest whose hashes do not describe the files beside it, which is the one
# claim vendoring exists to make. CI runs on Linux and would never see it.
#
# `-text` disables the translation for these paths while leaving them diffable.
vendor/openhack/** -text
